# Production Environment Variables Setup Guide

## FRONTEND (Vercel) Environment Variables:
# Add these in Vercel Project Settings → Environment Variables

REACT_APP_API_URL=https://your-backend-app.onrender.com/api
REACT_APP_NAME=Smart Video Learning

## BACKEND (Render) Environment Variables:
# Add these in Render Dashboard → Environment

PORT=10000
NODE_ENV=production
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://<username>:<password>@cluster.mongodb.net/smart-video-learning?retryWrites=true&w=majority
JWT_SECRET=<generate-a-strong-random-secret-here>
OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-proj-your-openai-api-key-here
YOUTUBE_API_KEY=your-youtube-api-key-here
CLIENT_URL=https://your-frontend-app.vercel.app
USE_MOCK_AI=false

# IMPORTANT NOTES:
# 1. Replace <username>, <password> with your MongoDB Atlas credentials
# 2. Generate a strong JWT_SECRET (use: openssl rand -base64 32)
# 3. Update CLIENT_URL with your actual Vercel deployment URL
# 4. Update REACT_APP_API_URL with your actual Render deployment URL
# 5. Port 10000 is commonly used by Render (they may override it)
